(
F5 W1 U6: control_input with a mesh extension (Professional 02-08-2026
 probe): 1.dat = "node 5 0 2 node 6 1 2 element 2 -quad4 3 4 5 6 end_data"
 (build_safe.sh, isolated directory); the nodes 5 and 6 are fixed by
 bounda_dof 3. The second step stretches the new element: node 5 sigyy
 20 (= Professional 02-08-2026). The integration-point state of the new
 element starts from the node values in the GNU (as for every element a
 mesh operation adds); the Professional starts it otherwise, so the shared
 nodes 3 and 4 average to sigyy -10 in the GNU and -5 in the Professional
 (DIVERGENCES CTRL-INPUT-NEWELEM, class C).)
echo -no
number_of_space_dimensions 2
materi_velocity
materi_strain_total
materi_stress
end_initia
node 1 0 0
node 2 1 0
node 3 0 1
node 4 1 1
element 1 -quad4 1 2 3 4
group_type 0 -materi
group_materi_elasti_young 0 1000
group_materi_elasti_poisson 0 0.
group_materi_memory 0 -updated_linear
bounda_dof 0 -ra 1 2 -ra -vely
bounda_dof 1 -ra 1 3 -ra -velx
bounda_dof 2 -ra 3 4 -ra -vely
bounda_time 2 0 0 2 -0.02
control_timestep 0 1 1
control_timestep 2 1 1
control_input 1 -yes
bounda_dof 3 -ra 5 6 -ra -velx -vely
target_item 0 -node_dof 5 -sigyy
target_value 0 20. 1.e-6
target_item 1 -node_dof 6 -sigyy
target_value 1 20. 1.e-6
end_data
